      "title": "چهارم (chahârom) — fourth, with nothing bending",
      "headword": "چهارم",
      "romanization": "chahârom",
      "gloss": "fourth — the rule applied with nothing bending at all",
      "script": "perso-arabic",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:35c3f66de09bba39",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say the ordinal ending, then dovvom and sevvom."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know first — one word",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "چهارم — chahârom — fourth."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "chahâr + -om, and nothing happens at the join. panjom, \"fifth,\" is the same: the cardinal ends in a consonant, so the ending simply follows it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dovvom and sevvom doubled a consonant only because their cardinals end in a vowel. Two and three are the exception; four onwards is the rule, all the way up. dahom is \"tenth\", bistom is \"twentieth\", sadom is \"hundredth.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So a reader who has twelve cardinals and one ending has twelve ordinals, minus the borrowed first."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "chahârom — fourth",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: **chahârom** — fourth]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "BUILD",
              "instruction": "panj + -om becomes panjom, fifth",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU BUILD: *panj* + *-om* → **panjom**, fifth]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "BUILD",
              "instruction": "dah + -om becomes dahom, tenth",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU BUILD: *dah* + *-om* → **dahom**, tenth]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sources: Wiktionary: چهارم (chahârom); Omniglot, Numbers in Persian."
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "FA-C20-chaharom-build",
              "prompt": "Build tenth and twentieth from dah and bist.",
              "assesses": [
                "FA-MORPH-ORDINAL-OM"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 14,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "dahom bistom",
                "dahom, bistom",
                "dahom and bistom"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "The ending never changes above three.",
                "incorrect": "Add -om: dahom, bistom."
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
